# 6. GITHUB STATE DETECTION

Determine whether the SaaS already has a GitHub repository.

## Case A — Existing repository

Verify:

```bash
git status
git remote -v
git branch --show-current
git fetch origin
git ls-remote --heads origin main
```

Then determine whether local and remote `main` are synchronized.

Never use:

```bash
git push --force
git reset --hard
git branch -D
```

in the generated normal deployment workflow unless explicitly required and separately approved.

---

## Case B — No GitHub repository

Generate a one-time setup procedure:

```text
INITIAL_GITHUB_SETUP.md
```

It must explain:

```bash
git init
git branch -M main
git add .
git commit -m "Initial commit"
git remote add origin <REPOSITORY_URL>
git push -u origin main
```

Before the first commit, verify that sensitive files are excluded.

