# 7. SECRET SCANNING — MANDATORY

Before every production deployment, scan the repository and build inputs for secrets.

Detect at minimum:

```text
API keys
private keys
tokens
passwords
database credentials
service-role credentials
JWT secrets
OAuth secrets
webhook secrets
payment secrets
deployment tokens
Vercel tokens
Supabase access tokens
GitHub tokens
cloud credentials
```

Scan:

```text
source
Git history when feasible
configuration
JSON
YAML
TS/JS
environment files
shell scripts
documentation
generated files
build artifacts
```

Never print detected secret values.

Output:

```text
SECRET DETECTED
Location
Type
Severity
Remediation
```

If a real secret is found in a tracked file or artifact:

```text
BLOCK
```

Do not automatically expose, copy, or rotate the secret.

