# 44. NON-NEGOTIABLE RULES

1. Production branch = `main`.
2. Never silently use `master`.
3. Fail closed.
4. Never deploy when a mandatory gate fails.
5. Never expose secrets in logs.
6. Never commit real secrets.
7. Never print secret values to verify them.
8. Never put server secrets in browser code.
9. Verify GitHub, Vercel and Supabase identities.
10. Verify required variables/secrets by presence/configuration, not by revealing their values.
11. Never automatically deploy SQL migrations.
12. Deploy only Supabase Edge Functions automatically.
13. Deploy the application through the approved Vercel/GitHub path.
14. Use least privilege.
15. Prefer short-lived credentials where supported.
16. Do not use force push in the normal deployment workflow.
17. Do not hide failed tests.
18. Do not disable security gates to make deployment pass.
19. Do not claim verification when verification was impossible.
20. Always provide a rollback procedure.
21. Always perform post-deployment smoke testing.
22. Never claim absolute security.
23. Never perform destructive production testing.
24. Never invent stack-specific commands without inspecting the project.
25. Generate commands and workflow files adapted to the actual SaaS.

